  "text": "Title: Bio Bay\n\nTHAT NIGHT WHEN WE tied up to a buoy in the middle of Bio Bay, the only sign of change \nI saw was a few streetlights on the hills to the north, not yet so much competition that \nthe planktonic glow was diminished. Otherwise, everything was exactly as it had been on my\nfirst visit five years ago. The constellation Orion still dominated the southern sky, the \nold hunter holding up his animal-skin shield (\"Uh, yeah, I think I see it\"), forever poised \nto clash with his bullet-headed foe Taurus. \nThen those of us who wished slipped quietly into the water.",
